{
  "id": "base-set-disco-holo-test-print",
  "name": "Base Set disco holo test print",
  "category": "test",
  "description": {
    "text": "Test prints of the Base Set holos in a holofoil pattern never used on any released Pokémon card. Collectors call it \"disco\", CGC's name for it, since it has no official one. Apart from the foil the cards follow the Shadowless print, with no 1st Edition stamp, but some design elements are missing. One of the two or three known uncut sheets has a pressman's sign-off dated January 21, 1999, twelve days after Base Set came out, and uses the later Unlimited sheet layout, so it wasn't a prototype for Base Set; CGC suggests Wizards of the Coast was trying foils for later print runs or sets. Former Wizards lead typesetter Chris Nitz recalled tests on \"a variety of available foil stocks\".\n\nThe cards were square cut from the sheets after they left the printer. CGC first authenticated one in June 2022 and has since graded every Base Set holo this way except Machamp, which was printed on a separate sheet. Counterfeits exist, singles and uncut sheets alike.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "CGC Cards: Extremely rare Base Set Charizard test print",
        "url": "https://www.cgccards.com/news/article/10283/test-print-charizard/"
      },
      {
        "title": "CGC Cards: Counterfeit \"Disco\" holo test print Charizard",
        "url": "https://www.cgccards.com/news/article/14311/"
      }
    ]
  },
